<title>JAPAN: Bridgestone to raise output in Asia -- paper.</title>
<headline>Bridgestone to raise output in Asia -- paper.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bridgestone Corp plans to invest a total of 26 billion yen to boost tyre production in Indonesia and Thailand due to rising demand in those countries and neighbouring nations, a Japanese daily said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The business daily Nikkan Kogyo Shimbun said that Bridgestone would start building a new plant in Indonesia in 1997 which would be capable of producing 40 tonnes of tyres a day. The company will also double its output in Thailand to 80 tonnes a day by the end of 1998, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>A spokesman for Bridgestone was not immediately available for comment.</p>
</text>
